# Ask before deleting significant content or features

**Rule:** Check with the user before deleting any significant content or feature.

Do not remove or strip meaningful behavior, copy, or structure without **explicit confirmation in the same conversation** (unless the user already asked you to remove that exact thing).

## What counts as significant (ask first)

- User-visible text, instructions, or instructional content
- Whole pages, major sections, routes, or navigation entries
- Code that implements a **feature** (UI behavior, APIs, scripts, styling that defines layout or branding)
- Shared or referenced assets, data, config, or helpers other parts of the project rely on
- Tests, tooling, or scripts that affect how the project runs or is verified

## What you can remove without asking

- Obvious mistakes you just introduced (duplicate lines, broken markup, wrong paste)
- Truly unused dead code **only if** you can show it is unreferenced in the same change (e.g. orphaned import)

## How to ask

State briefly what you plan to delete and why, then wait for approval. If unsure whether something is significant, **treat it as significant** and ask.
